< {"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":2,"result":{"tools":[{"name":"status","title":"Logic Pro status","description":"Whether Kumi's bridge in Logic Pro is connected: the Logic Pro and bridge versions, the open project, and whether Logic Pro is busy (a dialog, a render). With several Logic Pro instances running, pass pid or resource from discover.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"pid":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"description":"The Logic Pro process to use, from discover, when several run."},"resource":{"type":"string","description":"The Logic Pro to use, by its bundle id (com.apple.logic10) from discover, when several run."}},"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":true,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false}},{"name":"discover","title":"Find running Logic Pro","description":"Every running Logic Pro with Kumi's bridge: process id, port, resource folder, versions, open project, and whether it answers. Use it when status reports none, or to choose among several.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{},"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":true,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false}},{"name":"read","title":"Read Logic Pro","description":"Rows of one kind from the open Logic Pro project, a page at a time: {items, nextCursor?, epoch}. Pass parent (a row's ref) to read what is inside it, such as a track's items or an FX's parameters; pass the previous page's nextCursor as cursor for the next page. Or pass ref alone for the one object it names. Refs hold until the epoch changes. With several Logic Pro instances running, pass pid or resource from discover.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"pid":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"description":"The Logic Pro process to use, from discover, when several run."},"resource":{"type":"string","description":"The Logic Pro to use, by its bundle id (com.apple.logic10) from discover, when several run."},"kind":{"type":"string","enum":["project","track","region","note","plugin","send","marker","tempo"],"description":"What to read in Logic Pro."},"parent":{"type":"string","description":"The ref of what the rows are in: a track for its regions, plug-ins or sends; a region for its notes (required for notes)."},"ref":{"type":"string","description":"The ref of one object to read instead of a page of rows."},"cursor":{"type":"string","description":"The nextCursor an earlier page gave, unchanged."},"limit":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"maximum":200,"description":"Rows in a page (50 by default)."}},"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":true,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false}},{"name":"snapshot","title":"Logic Pro snapshot","description":"The open Logic Pro project on one screen: {epoch, project, transport, tracks, selection, markers?}. What is too big to include is named under truncated, to read with `read`.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"pid":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"description":"The Logic Pro process to use, from discover, when several run."},"resource":{"type":"string","description":"The Logic Pro to use, by its bundle id (com.apple.logic10) from discover, when several run."}},"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":true,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false}},{"name":"focus","title":"Logic Pro focus","description":"What the producer is looking at in Logic Pro: {epoch, view, selection, transport, changed}. Cheap enough to poll about every 150 ms; read again only when changed moves.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"pid":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"description":"The Logic Pro process to use, from discover, when several run."},"resource":{"type":"string","description":"The Logic Pro to use, by its bundle id (com.apple.logic10) from discover, when several run."}},"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":true,"idempotentHint":false,"openWorldHint":false}},{"name":"focus_body","title":"Logic Pro view","description":"What Logic Pro shows in one of its views, ready to draw: pass kind, and ref (the take, track or pattern it is about) or window (the range to show) where the kind takes them. Long ones come in pages: pass the nextCursor as cursor.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"pid":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"description":"The Logic Pro process to use, from discover, when several run."},"resource":{"type":"string","description":"The Logic Pro to use, by its bundle id (com.apple.logic10) from discover, when several run."},"kind":{"type":"string","enum":["tree","notes","timeline","routing"],"description":"Which view."},"ref":{"type":"string","description":"The ref of what the view is about: a track for tree and routing, a region for notes (the selected one when left out)."},"around":{"type":"string","description":"The ref of a track to centre the first page of the timeline's lanes on: the page starts half a page above it, and says where in `from`."},"window":{"type":"object","properties":{"from":{"type":"number"},"to":{"type":"number"}},"required":["from","to"],"additionalProperties":false,"description":"The range of the timeline to show, in beats from the project's start."},"cursor":{"type":"string","description":"The nextCursor an earlier page gave, unchanged."},"limit":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"maximum":200,"description":"Rows in a page."}},"required":["kind"],"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":true,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false}}]}}
